body:
Maybe it's not the best example, but this triggers error as well. Error occurs in any cases of the incomplete DOCTYPE, e.g. `<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC>`, `<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "something>`. On the other hand now I think we should add additional error codes:
- `<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC>` will be a `missing-doctype-public-identifier` parse error;
- `<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "fdjkj>` will be a `abrupt-doctype-public-identifier` parse error;

and two more errors for the system identifiers.
